# Lunduke Linux Kernel config delta: 7.2.6-lcos14 → 7.2.6-lcos15
# Built 2026-10-06 — config and packaging only; no kernel debs, no ISO bake.
#
# Base is the lcos14 config (6487b4dc). lcos12, lcos13, and lcos14 files
# are not edited. This file is the full lcos14 → lcos15 delta (ASIX, TUN, KVM).
# olddefconfig: Linux 7.2.6, gcc-14, LOCALVERSION= (same finalize as the
# build script). A second olddefconfig on the saved config kept every
# requested module. The only line it dropped was "# CONFIG_RUST is not set",
# which scripts/config --disable RUST appends again.
#
# Intentional hardware and features (modules):
#   CONFIG_USB_NET_AX88179_178A=m
#     LCOS issue 100. Module ax88179_178a. Vendor-class only:
#       0b95:1790 class ff/ff/00 — ASIX AX88179
#       0b95:178a class ff/ff/00 — ASIX AX88178A
#   CONFIG_USB_NET_AX8817X=m
#     Module asix. Older AX88172 / AX88772 / AX88772A / AX88772B / AX88178.
#   CONFIG_USB_NET_CDC_NCM=m
#     Module cdc_ncm. Linux 7.2.6 has no AX88179A/AX88772D string.
#     Those chips share 0b95:1790 and a CDC-NCM configuration. cdc_ncm binds
#     USB_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_CLASS_COMM, USB_CDC_SUBCLASS_NCM,
#     USB_CDC_PROTO_NONE). usb core prefers that non-vendor config.
#     USB_NET_CDCETHER was already m.
#   CONFIG_TUN=m
#     LCOS issue 87 follow-up. Module tun. Rootless podman (pasta /
#     slirp4netns) needs /dev/net/tun. TUN selects CRC32, already y.
#     CONFIG_TUN_VNET_CROSS_LE stays unset.
#     MACVLAN, IPVLAN, VXLAN, DUMMY, and VLAN_8021Q stay unset.
#   CONFIG_KVM=m, CONFIG_KVM_INTEL=m, CONFIG_KVM_AMD=m
#     LCOS issue 103. Modules kvm, kvm-intel, kvm-amd. Intel and AMD hosts.
#     CONFIG_VIRTUALIZATION was already y. CONFIG_KVM_GUEST stays y
#     (guest support is separate from hosting).
#     CONFIG_VFIO stays unset. CONFIG_VHOST_NET stays unset.
#     No other VHOST_* host driver was enabled.
#
# No firmware request in the ASIX, cdc_ncm, tun, or kvm drivers.
# No firmware blob is added.
#
# ASIX dependency fill (first olddefconfig):
#   USB_NET_AX8817X selects PHYLINK=m, which selects SWPHY=y.
#   PHYLIB, CRC32, AX88796B_PHY, NET_SELFTESTS were already set.
#   Newly visible and left off: CONFIG_SFP.
#
# KVM/TUN dependency fill (second olddefconfig, on the ASIX lcos15):
#   KVM_INTEL selects X86_FRED=y (X86_64). That drops the derived markers
#   X86_REQUIRED_FEATURE_SYSFAST32 and X86_DISABLED_FEATURE_FRED.
#   KVM_X86 (def_tristate of KVM once a vendor module is set) selects the
#   HAVE_KVM_* / KVM_* internal bools, KVM_GUEST_MEMFD, VHOST_TASK,
#   USER_RETURN_NOTIFIER, GUEST_PERF_EVENTS, PERF_GUEST_MEDIATED_PMU,
#   PREEMPT_NOTIFIERS (via KVM_COMMON), and HAVE_KVM_IRQ_BYPASS=m which
#   selects IRQ_BYPASS_MANAGER=m.
#   KVM_VFIO=y is that internal bool. It is not CONFIG_VFIO. VFIO stays unset.
#   VHOST_TASK=y is the KVM helper bool. It is not a vhost host driver.
#   VHOST_NET and VHOST_VSOCK stay unset.
#   Because CONFIG_WERROR=y, KVM_X86 selects KVM_WERROR=y.
#   New symbols with default y, kept:
#     KVM_IOAPIC, KVM_SMM, KVM_HYPERV,
#     KVM_AMD_SEV (CRYPTO_DEV_SP_PSP was already y; selects
#       ARCH_HAS_CC_PLATFORM and the GMEM prepare/invalidate/populate
#       symbols, and drops X86_DISABLED_FEATURE_SEV_SNP),
#     KVM_MAX_NR_VCPUS=1024,
#     MITIGATION_VMSCAPE (depends on KVM, default y).
#   Newly visible and left off (default n): CONFIG_KVM_XEN.
#
# Debian 7.2.6 amd64 USB Ethernet drivers that stay off are listed in
# docs/lcos15-module-verify.txt.
#
# CRITICAL: # CONFIG_RUST is not set (No Forced Rust).
# olddefconfig drops that comment when RUST_IS_AVAILABLE=n (rustc 1.83 is
# below Linux 7.2.6's 1.85 minimum, and bindgen is absent). The snapshot
# appends the comment again with scripts/config --disable RUST.
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-lunduke".
#
# Unified diff of full .config follows.
#
